        "text": "107"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000003",
    "raw_sha256": "a11ebf3d10ee7348d5a2d69e360512f5a51e183dc728273391516fb51c5d2e81",
    "page_line_sha256": "36266cc81c09ccfbab9c9450da00731a459dd941c3f7baca52e7390ace7e838f",
    "lines": [
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000003",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 24,
        "text": "39th Cong. ... 1st Sess."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000004",
    "raw_sha256": "df52dd6a1e8214ac764d3abb387adcae88465e2b92f0127dd010fce7d7fb3659",
    "page_line_sha256": "36266cc81c09ccfbab9c9450da00731a459dd941c3f7baca52e7390ace7e838f",
    "lines": [
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000004",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 48,
        "text": "Apportionment of Bepresentation — Mr. Henderson."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000005",
    "raw_sha256": "b51915008655401f5b78157cfc0480d0282c0f8db8ca2238b3a07a5362b9c3d1",
    "page_line_sha256": "36266cc81c09ccfbab9c9450da00731a459dd941c3f7baca52e7390ace7e838f",
    "lines": [
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000005",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 7,
        "text": "Senate."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000006",
    "raw_sha256": "f77d6de4e79ea615bc7c3a4823987f768a829a9c452386c87a3605007eb2b678",
    "page_line_sha256": "36266cc81c09ccfbab9c9450da00731a459dd941c3f7baca52e7390ace7e838f",
    "lines": [
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000006",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 46,
        "text": "He cannot give a license or indulgence to com-"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000007",
        "start": 47,
        "end": 94,
        "text": "mit crime ; but after a crime is committed, all"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000008",
        "start": 95,
        "end": 145,
        "text": "he has to do in his certificate is to specify par-"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000009",
        "start": 146,
        "end": 189,
        "text": "ticularly the crime that has been committed"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000010",
        "start": 190,
        "end": 233,
        "text": "and for which the pardon is granted. But it"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000011",
        "start": 234,
        "end": 281,
        "text": "may well be denied that but for the act of Con-"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000012",
        "start": 282,
        "end": 329,
        "text": "gress of July 17, 18G2, of which my friend from"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000013",
        "start": 330,
        "end": 369,
        "text": "New Hampshire before me [Mr. Clark] was"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000014",
        "start": 370,
        "end": 414,
        "text": "perhaps the chief draughtsman, the President"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000015",
        "start": 415,
        "end": 458,
        "text": "would have any authority to grant a general"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000016",
        "start": 459,
        "end": 504,
        "text": "pardon or amnestj\\ I must admit that that act"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000017",
        "start": 505,
        "end": 554,
        "text": "is quite full. Let me refer to it. The thirteenth"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000018",
        "start": 555,
        "end": 582,
        "text": "section is in these words :"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000007",
    "raw_sha256": "b4f4cd8ccce9ffb5f813c7435c7ff3cff6b6056c74c42378c418b40a9e01821b",
    "page_line_sha256": "36266cc81c09ccfbab9c9450da00731a459dd941c3f7baca52e7390ace7e838f",
    "lines": [
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000019",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 52,
        "text": "\"Sec. 13. And he it further enacted. That the Presi-"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000020",
        "start": 53,
        "end": 106,
        "text": "dent is hereby .authorized, at any time hereafter, by"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000021",
        "start": 107,
        "end": 154,
        "text": "proclamation, to extend to persons who may have"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000022",
        "start": 155,
        "end": 209,
        "text": "participated in the existing rebellion in any State or"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000023",
        "start": 210,
        "end": 260,
        "text": "part thereof, pardon and amnesty, with such excep-"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000024",
        "start": 261,
        "end": 312,
        "text": "tions and at such time and on such conditions as he"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000025",
        "start": 313,
        "end": 356,
        "text": "may deem expedient for the public welfare.\""
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "source_id": "congressionalglo7395unit:741:par_000741_000008",
    "raw_sha256": "31abb50be6f0b3553bdca7e9b8103b0ada437fd2cb57e49d22db61ab40c2646e",
    "page_line_sha256": "36266cc81c09ccfbab9c9450da00731a459dd941c3f7baca52e7390ace7e838f",
    "lines": [
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000026",
        "start": 0,
        "end": 46,
        "text": "It will not be disputed that by virtue of that"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000027",
        "start": 47,
        "end": 93,
        "text": "authority the President had power to issue his"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000028",
        "start": 94,
        "end": 139,
        "text": "proclamation of general amnesty. But disputes"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000029",
        "start": 140,
        "end": 183,
        "text": "may arise on other questions connected with"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000030",
        "start": 184,
        "end": 230,
        "text": "this proclamation. What was the condition upon"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000031",
        "start": 231,
        "end": 278,
        "text": "which the pardon was to inure to the benefit of"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000032",
        "start": 279,
        "end": 326,
        "text": "the party pardoned? It was first that he should"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000033",
        "start": 327,
        "end": 370,
        "text": "file the oath named and in the manner to be"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000034",
        "start": 371,
        "end": 420,
        "text": "prescribed. But this is not of itself sufficient."
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000035",
        "start": 421,
        "end": 463,
        "text": "There is something more necessary that the"
      },
      {
        "line_id": "line_000741_000036",
        "start": 464,
        "end": 500,
        "text": "benefits of the pardon should inure."
      }
    ]
  }
]
